# rm546, the gutter-mark star (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm546
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_roald_wickstack
written_by codex
title the gutter-mark star
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=servant
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=devout drive=steady
quirk inks_a_star_beside_the_first_flooded_turn
likes spiced_cider stars fresh_straw first_snow
dislikes crowds smoke
fears sending_a_loaded_cart_to_a_drowned_turning
hopes for_a_market_stand_above_high_water
topics weather +0.5 work +0.4 faith +0.4 prices +0.2
styles comfort=steady gossip=plain refuse=firm tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# inks a star beside the first flooded turning and keeps the small street sketch folded inside a cuff.

words
oath! = By the inked star | High sill and dry straw
saying! = Mark where the water turns first | One star for the street that goes under
map = my cuff map | a small sketched turning
star = the five-pointed mark | the black ink star
straw = a dry straw wisp | a short golden stalk
ink = my stained forepaw | an ink-dark fingertip
sill = the high sill | a clean stone doorstep
cider = a little spiced cider | a fragrant warm draught
clove = the bruised clove | a bit of fragrant spice
snow = the year's first dusting | an early white covering
till = my stall purse | a little roll of coppers
smoke = an ugly smoke smear | a dirty patch of air
cart = the laden handcart | a low market truck
rill = a narrow runnel | a busy strip of gutter water

any
opinion @1 church for 2 : A dry turning under my neighbour's load deserves a grateful prayer. I can mark it on paper as well as giving thanks.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : Carry a meal round the high way before deciding a flooded street is reason enough to leave it cold.
opinion @1 festivals against 1 : In a crush I can't even see the water at my own feet. The bells may travel here without the crowd.
opinion @1 merchants against 1 : A narrow gutter doesn't double the journey. I'm apt to question a price that says otherwise.
opinion @1 drink against 1 : Spice is what I like in a winter cup. I've seen good company washed away by what's poured afterwards.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Come up by the high step. | Welcome past the trickle.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes] : You've caught me beside the dry bundles. | Mind the folded map under my cuff.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning keeps a clear edge on the gutter. | A fresh sky above the paving.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. I can still see our footing. | Come in under a star or two.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Household company gets the drier chair. | Good to see a home face past the puddles.
line @1 again.open : Here we are on the high part again. | There's another turn in our talk.
line @1 greet.return : Welcome back to a dry crossing. | Your feet found a sound way here.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : I'd mark your doorstep with a welcome star. | Friendly faces brighten this high ground.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : My hands are stained but free. | This dry end of the passage will do.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Welcome by the lamp above the flood mark. | A familiar step after the stars come out.
line @1 farewell : Keep above the first wet turning. | Dry cuffs when your last gate opens.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll remember the crossing for you. | Find a sound route for your next errand.
line @2 farewell.return [here.time=night] : Bright stars above a safe homeward path. | May your last doorstep stand clear.
line @1 react.news : Which turn has that report taken? | Tell me the part worth writing beside a star.
line @1 react.news.new : My map had no mark for that yet. | A new report under these eaves.
line @1 react.news.known : That came by the high road yesterday. | I've already a mark beside that word.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'd walk to the turning before marking a flood quite that deep. | Some tales run downhill faster than the water itself.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : An ugly turning. I'll wait here with you. | Bring your burden over onto this dry bit.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That's a star to put in good ink. | A heartening arrival by any road.
line @1 ask.how : What sort of crossing did you get today? | Have you had a dry hour for yourself?
line @1 answer.how : My cuffs are dry and my prayers are said. | Some ink on my paws, enough hope in my pocket.
line @1 decline : I'd sooner keep the light for the other route I promised to check. | I must leave my spare hour open for a household errand.
line @1 accept_decline : No black star beside that answer. | The matter stands where you left it.
line @1 thank : You kept a troublesome bit of work dry. | That help will go in my evening thanks.
line @1 sympathise : Take a steady breath by this high sill. | I'll stay where you can see a friendly face.
line @1 reassure : A little higher ground can change the whole view. | We can set out when the water falls.
line @1 preclose : I'd best take one more look at that gutter. | There is a folding sum waiting in my cuff.
scene star
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #map.capitalize# gets #star# at the first turn a shower takes for its own.
b : One star only? | Why that turn?
a : Another for the next heavy rain if it begins somewhere else. I keep the dates small. | A cart sent the wrong way loses its whole load before any grand flood is declared.

scene wisp
when topic=work self.job=servant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I lay #straw# by a threshold when there's water coming down the lane.
b : A test? | Does it always work?
a : If it swims indoors the sill needs attention before I carry in another dry bundle. | It gives a plain warning. I still have to look at what actually comes under the door.

scene fingers
when topic=work self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's a little black ink in the fur between my toes where I steadied the street sketch.
b : Can't it wash out? | Do you mind?
a : Eventually. I usually need to amend the map before the last mark has entirely faded. | More if it lands on household linen. I keep a proper cloth round my drawing hand.

scene faith
when topic=faith self.piety=devout
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put down a star with ink after a prayer for sure footing.
b : Why both? | Is the prayer enough?
a : Because I happen to have ink as well as time to pray. A traveller can use the mark immediately. | Enough for my heart. The traveller may need an actual dry street.

scene cider
when topic=food self.likes=spiced_cider
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep #clove# in #cider# till its little shadow stops turning.
b : Then drink? | Why the shadow?
a : A comfortable sip. Too hot at first and too pleasant to forget entirely. | Spice turns sharply in a moving cup. I've a fondness for reading currents in small things.

scene stars
when topic=pastimes self.likes=stars
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The first star after rain sometimes has a second small self in the gutter.
b : Which do you watch? | Do you draw both?
a : The high one if I'm thinking, the low one if I've a bucket to carry. | Just the star beside the flooded road. My sketch already has enough things that aren't visible by day.

scene winter
when topic=weather self.likes=first_snow
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #snow.capitalize# shows the first warm water track before a street has quite decided to flood.
b : You can see that? | Is the snow spoiled?
a : A dark thread goes across new white. You needn't be a surveyor to take the hint. | At one crossing. Above it there's plenty white enough to cheer my morning.

scene crowds
when topic=festival self.dislikes=crowds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In a crowded street I can't see the step that takes water first.
b : Do you wait? | Why worry on a dry day?
a : I walk round. Time outdoors is cheaper than a full bucket overturned at the last moment. | I want room to find my own footing in any weather.

scene smoke
when topic=health self.dislikes=smoke
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #smoke.capitalize# hides the stars and makes the lights below spread out against the wet stones.
b : Which way then? | Do you stay in?
a : The familiar route with a sound kerb. A shining street isn't necessarily a dry one. | If the errands allow. A clear breath goes well with keeping the map up to date.

scene coins
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put another copper in #till# whenever my household wage allows it.
b : For what pitch? | A large stall?
a : For one that stays dry throughout a market day. I've a few corners under consideration. | Anything that will hold my goods and a stool above ankle water would make a strong beginning.

scene home
when topic=home self.street
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #self.street# has a different shape in my head before rain and after it.
b : Two maps? | What stays the same?
a : One page. A star and two tiny strokes will do more than a second whole drawing. | The way the highest lintel stands out against the evening sky. I can aim for that in almost any weather.

scene workplace
when topic=work self.workplace self.job=servant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I take dry straw to #self.workplace# by a route that looks needlessly long in clear weather.
b : Why that way today? | Does anyone ask?
a : I've learned the safe corners for carrying a full arm. I value the habit more than the minute it costs me. | If there's a question I show the sketch. They can see what happened the last time it rained.

scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd give #self.friend# a copy of the two stars that matter on a market errand.
b : Why only two? | Would you charge?
a : Too many little directions make a map hard to consult with wet fingers. | For a friend's safe footing? Ink doesn't cost me that much.

scene neighbour
when topic=home self.neighbour
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I could ask #self.neighbour# which doorway was last to dry out.
b : Would you take that as proof? | What if accounts differ?
a : As a reason to walk over myself. A doorstep can differ from the crossing below it. | Then two good questions have come out of one drawing. I like a map that can still be corrected.

scene anger
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When a delivery gets sent down a flooded lane I find my temper rising faster than the water.
b : What do you say? | How do you cool down?
a : Which way to come back with the load. Other remarks can wait for those bundles to dry. | Spread the map out. Angry paws can still point clearly at the next dry turn.

scene newcomer
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I show a stranger one high doorway before beginning an account of the whole quarter.
b : Why a doorway? | What comes next?
a : It's something to aim at while bringing an armful of belongings into an unfamiliar street. | Which turning keeps shoes out of water. Names and house histories can wait.

scene supper
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A dry chair under a hot meal is a luxury I've learned to count separately.
b : How many luxuries altogether? | Which would you lend?
a : A chair, a bowl, a dry floor and a companion with a decent appetite. Four things to be thankful for. | A neighbour who needed one could have my stool while I took the sill.

scene dream
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dreamed the whole sky was a street map with rain running from star to star.
b : Where did it drain? | Useful for errands?
a : Into the handle of my cider cup. I had to keep moving the cup to save the houses. | I woke with the route to breakfast very clear indeed. I wouldn't trust the rest without walking it.

story starstory [topic=memories]
  : My first ink star was supposed to be a dot. I put a paw into the wet mark and dragged five little points across the turn where the paving slopes.
  : In the rain I found the mistake easier to see than all my carefully rounded dots. It became the only sign I didn't have to explain to myself twice.
  b : Did you leave the paw mark?
  : I trimmed the longest point. The star still bears an honest relation to a careless morning.

story cupstory [topic=food]
  : I carried a warm spiced cup across a freshly swept floor while watching a dark line outside the sill. A clove went round and round in the cider.
  : From outside came a little straw going round the same way. I put the cup down and barred the lower door before either current could spill indoors.
  b : Did the drink go cold?
  : Just cool enough for the first real taste. My timings are seldom so fortunate.

story pitchstory [topic=prices]
  : I looked at a market pitch in sunshine once and very nearly spent my little savings to hold it. My eye kept catching on a dark band below its boards.
  : I came the next morning when the lane was wet. The band sat precisely along the upper margin of a muddy pool. I counted my coppers and put them all back.
  b : Have you chosen a better spot?
  : I've chosen a better hour to do my looking. A stall needs its first inspection after a good hard rain.

rule @aside1
when concept=bark self.job=servant self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Straw above the sill, first bundle dry. | Fold the route before lifting the bucket.

rule @aside2
when concept=bark self.likes=stars
does aside
cooldown 7h
say There's its twin in the gutter. | A dry sky in a very wet street.

rule @aside3
when concept=bark self.likes=spiced_cider
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The clove's almost come to rest. | A fine dark swirl of spice there.

rule @aside4
when concept=bark self.piety=devout
does aside
cooldown 9h
say A thankful word for these dry steps. | Ink for the map after a word of prayer.

dlg @1 resident.hub : Come onto the raised paving with me. I'll hear you while the little runnel finds its direction.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=servant self.workplace] : I'm in household service at #self.workplace#. Dry bundles take a good deal of thought in this city.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : This travelled clear of the flooded turns. #world.news#
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, room on the high step for a familiar caller.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Dry ground by the Bright One's favour all along your journey.
graft resident.hub
choice What does the star on your cuff map mean? -> cuff_star
node cuff_star
say It's the first street to take water in a hard rain. I draw the star big enough to find when the paper's wet and I've only one free thumb.
free
choice Why would a household servant keep that map? -> cuff_goods
choice I'll mind the marked turning. -> hub
node cuff_goods
say Ask a wet bundle of clean straw what the short route cost. Some day I mean to have my own market stand, and I'll know where to keep its feet dry.
choice I'd look at a pitch after rain too. -> hub
choice May the stand find sound ground. -> bye
